DHCP Server Configuration Using Your Commands

Step 1: Enter Privileged Mode

enable

Moves router to privileged EXEC mode.


---

Step 2: Enter Global Configuration Mode

configure terminal

Used to configure router settings.


---

Step 3: Configure Interface

interface FastEthernet0/0

Selects FastEthernet0/0 interface.


---

Step 4: Assign IP Address

ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0

Sets router IP address.


---

Step 5: Enable Interface

no shutdown

Activates the interface.


---

Step 6: Exit Interface Mode

exit

Returns to global configuration mode.


---

Step 7: Create DHCP Pool

ip dhcp pool mypool

Creates DHCP pool named mypool.


---

Step 8: Define Network

network 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0

Defines network range for DHCP clients.


---

Step 9: Configure Default Gateway

default-router 192.168.1.1

Sets router as default gateway.


---

Step 10: Configure DNS Server

dns-server 192.168.1.10

Assigns DNS server address.


---

Important Additional Command

Before creating DHCP pool, add:

ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.1.1

This prevents router IP from being assigned to clients.


---

Full Final Commands

enable
configure terminal

interface FastEthernet0/0
ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.1.1

ip dhcp pool mypool
network 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0
default-router 192.168.1.1
dns-server 192.168.1.10


---

PC Configuration

On PC:

Desktop → IP Configuration → DHCP

IP will be assigned automatically.


---

Verification Commands

show ip dhcp binding

Shows assigned IP addresses.


---

Short Viva Answers

What is DHCP?

DHCP automatically assigns IP addresses.


---

Why use DHCP?

To reduce manual IP configuration.


---

What is DHCP pool?

Range of IP addresses assigned to clients.


---

What is excluded-address?

Reserved IP that DHCP cannot assign.


---

Why use no shutdown?

To activate router interface.


---

DHCP Port Numbers?

Server → 67

Client → 68
